    "case_id": "347",
    "case_summary": "A teenaged boy presented with a 1-year history of asymptomatic cutaneous lesions on the face that had progressively spread to the trunk and extremities. He also experienced asthenia and mild intermittent arthralgias.\n\nMultiple millimetric erythematous to hyperpigmented monomorphic keratotic papules involving the head, trunk, and extremities. Symmetric annular brown erythematous plaques on the cheeks and temples were also seen. There were no vesicles or pustules.\n\n{'Laboratory Tests': ['- Normal white blood cell count', '- Mild anemia (hemoglobin level, 11.3 g/dL; normal level 12.50-15.50 g/dL)', '- Hypocomplementemia', '- Moderate proteinuria', '- Raised levels of antinuclear antibodies (>1:160)', '- Positive: anti-Smith antibodies, SSA/Ro antibodies, SSB/La antibodies, and anti-U1RNP antibodies', '- Negative: Anti-dsDNA antibodies, lupus anticoagulant, rheumatoid factor, IgG and IgM anticardiolipin antibody, and anti-β2 glycoprotein 1 antibody'], 'Histopathology': {'Biopsy Findings': 'Slightly atrophic epidermis with interface dermatitis, individual dyskeratotic keratinocytes, and a superficial perivascular and interstitial infiltrate of neutrophils, admixed with numerous mononuclear histiocytoid cells. Few eosinophils and leukocytoclastic debris were apparent, but there was no evidence of subepidermal blister formation or vasculitis.', 'Immunohistochemistry': 'Mononuclear histiocytoid cells showed immunoreactivity for myeloperoxidase and CD68', 'Direct Immunofluorescence': 'Negative results'}, 'Images': {'Figure A': 'Millimetric erythematous to hyperpigmented monomorphic papules involving the trunk', 'Figure B': 'Erythematous papules and symmetric annular brown erythematous plaques on the cheeks and temples', 'Figure C and D': 'Punch biopsy results (hematoxylin-eosin)'}}",
